			"date": "2026-08-31T14:16:20.589Z",
			"content": "<p>ah, so I hadn’t realized that <a href=\"https://adobe.com\">adobe.com</a> was client-rendered <a href=\"https://www.speedlify.dev/site/www-adobe-com/#without-javascript\">www.speedlify.dev/site/www-ado...</a></p>\n<p>I added a warning in speedlify2 for that.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf5rc5do22p",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf3t5x5j22e",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social/post/3muf5rc5do22p",
			"author": {
				"name": "Duffeh",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/bafkreihf42m7kegjr2iu7zucmfcby4dqblokuc7ii3nomjtfv7tod5m6la"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T14:51:05.359Z",
			"content": "<p>Yeah it looks to be what Adobe claim is the \"future of frontend\" called EDS, which is a client side render, for pages that could be static generated.</p>\n<p>They talk a lot about perfect lighthouse score, at what seems like a cost to real users. The header is a tell they load that last for some reason.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf6dx2c522p",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:gvi5yecbeb6e6oc32kbx35jl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mu6cybb4rc2z",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social/post/3muf6dx2c522p",
			"author": {
				"name": "Duffeh",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/bafkreihf42m7kegjr2iu7zucmfcby4dqblokuc7ii3nomjtfv7tod5m6la"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T15:01:31.260Z",
			"content": "<p>They do a lot of rubbish like this as a part of their new framework sadly.</p>\n<p>The initial html the LCP image likely has loading='lazy' and in JavaScript they will change it to loading eager to make lighthouse \"happy\".</p>\n<p>Adobe is just a perfect example of what not to do.n</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
